# zed-mcp-server-zai-web-reader local config — the template for `.env` (gitignored, NEVER commit).
#
# Copy:  cp .env.example .env   then fill in values.
# Nothing in this repo auto-loads `.env`. This is a Zed extension (WASM):
# it reads NO environment variables itself — the API key comes from Zed
# settings, and the extension hands it to the MCP server process it spawns.
# The entries below document that hand-off; values here are inert unless you
# run the MCP server by hand.

# ── Z.ai API key (web-reader) ────────────────────────────
# What: your Z.ai API key.
# Used by: src/*.rs context_server_command() — read from the Zed setting
#   `zai_api_key` (configuration/default_settings.jsonc), NOT from env.
#   Passed to the spawned supergateway (Node) as CLI args `--oauth2Bearer <key>` (no env var) for https://api.z.ai/api/mcp/web_reader/mcp.
# Where it normally lives: Zed settings.json →
#   "context_servers": { "mcp-server-zai-web-reader": { "settings": { "zai_api_key": "..." } } }
# Get: https://z.ai/manage-apikey/apikey-list
# Required for the MCP server to authenticate (empty → no key is passed).
# No env var exists for it: the key travels only as the --oauth2Bearer CLI
# argument, so there is nothing to set here — configure it in Zed settings.

# ── GitHub Actions secret (CI only — NOT read locally) ─────────────────────
# COMMITTER_TOKEN: GitHub PAT that lets huacnlee/zed-extension-action push the
#   release to katopz/extensions (push-to in release.yml).
# Used by: .github/workflows/release.yml (on `v*` tags).
# Get: GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Personal access tokens, with
#   repo/PR write on katopz/extensions.
# Set: repo Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions (not in this file).
# Required only for tag releases.
# COMMITTER_TOKEN=
